In keeping with the tradition of adding legendary weapons as artifacts
(Tsurugi of Muramasa, Excalibur, Mjollnir, Grayswandir, etc), I propose
adding a few others.

1) Kusanagi, chaotic short sword (wakizashi)

     This blade was found by Susanowo when he slew Orochi, the 8-headed
dragon. He then gifted it to Amaterasu to redress an earlier wrong,
after which it found its way back to earth.

    Effects when wielded: grants poison resistance (one meaning for the
word 'Kusanagi' is sword of snake), fire resistance.
    On hit: +d5 to hit, double damage versus dragons, snakes and
lizards, 25% chance to scare air elementals and vortices on successful
hit. (One of Kusanagi's powers is the ability to control wind and air).

2) Kanajana, neutral long sword

    (From Moorcock's Eternal Champion series, as the weapon of Erekose)
    When wielded: sheds light (like Sunsword).
     On hit: +d5 to hit, deals 1d6 extra damage to all enemies. Double
damage versus humanoids (all @, h, G plus nurses and lycanthropes. Also
versus Doppelgangers, Drow etc in [S]). 5% chance of an instakill
versus non-neutral @s. (the radiation that Kanajana emits, per the
book, can be deadly to humans)

3) Twinkle, chaotic scimitar

     (One of the weapons of Drizzt Do'Urden from R.A. Salvatore's
Forgotten Realms books. Possibly a copyright problem, alas, but if it's
not...)
    When wielded: Warning versus lawful foes, protection equal to
enchantment.
    On hit: +d5 to hit, extra 1d8 damage if two-weaponed in primary
hand or +2 to AC if in secondary hand, double damage to (master) mind
flayers.

4) Katana of Masamune, lawful katana

     (From Japanese myth)
    When wielded: bisection/decapitation resistance (the Katana of
Masamune parries the fatal slash!)
    On hit: +d5 to hit, may (5% chance) destroy enemy's (non-artifact)
weapon, double damage if opponent is wielding a weapon.



